# Types

Fix the design; don't silence the compiler. Escape hatch = design bug.
Do not add suppressions just to pass CI.

Prefer: sum types over parallel booleans; the repo's fallible-op idiom
(Result, error returns, checked exceptions — match neighbors);
explicit public signatures; schema-inferred types when schemas exist;
one nullish convention per repo.

Language bans (`any`, blind casts, unwrap, ignored errors) live in
TOOLCHAIN.md / Semgrep / Clippy when present — not re-stated here.
